# Current queue admission review

The exact source d61d6879 passed 45 real PostgreSQL 18.6 cases and 66 top-level
component tests with race instrumentation on Linux amd64. Its full Control
modules, make check, make build and configuration/HTTP platform tests passed.
The same source passed those four broad phases on macOS arm64. Both use Go1.27.3
and offline dependencies. No browser test ran.

The component namespace had no default IPv4/IPv6 route and the PostgreSQL
container had no network or published port. The separate fresh/dump/restore
catalog harness was explicitly excluded; this change introduces no production
DDL. Temporary database, secret files and relay were cleaned up.

The macOS platform's first run could not retain setgid bits because the private
scratch directory inherited group wheel. Assigning only that owned scratch
directory to the invoking user's group preserved mode2600. The same unmodified
tests passed on retry. Both original failure and successful retry logs are kept.

The native source remains pinned at refs/codex/sch-current-qualified/d61d6879.
An integration head may differ only in documentation before publication.
The candidate patch, ancestry and actual accepted main must be refreshed and
recorded before the packet is sealed. UNPUBLISHED means no publication claim.

The configured 10,000-workspace fixture held exactly two advisory lock tags;
it is not the SCH111 node/job admission load test. No production schema, native
serving-role grant, real eligible-batch/priority owner, all-writer cutover,
authenticated dispatcher, installed controller or UI flow is qualified here.
SCH103 and other product boxes remain open. The new research records preemption,
